 "ranks": "author-top-cards overnight, 2026-11-17/18 (23:55 to 10:00): the triaged cards past EDHREC rank 13,500 in rank order, Zevlor, Elturel Exile (13560) to Hedonist's Trove (17788), each with the small key it waited on, built by 34 worktree agents one lane at a time (build-family's overnight lanes loop), the concurrency varied by phase for the user's experiment (6, 4, 2, then 5 at once). 171 cards (178 definitions with the double-faced cards' backs), among them Zevlor, Wan Shi Tong, Kraven the Hunter, Aeon Engine, Invasion Plans, Ertai's Meddling, Murktide Regent, Gather Specimens, Hallowed Moonlight, Order of Succession and Battletide Alchemist; about a third needed no engine code. Re-keyed and built the same night: Glyph of Life (trigger:dealt-damage-by-attacking-creature), Ludevic, Necrogenius (replacement:as-transforms-copy-exiled-choice), Hallowed Moonlight (replacement:token-enter-exile-instead), Protective Sphere (effect:prevent-chosen-source-sharing-spent-mana-color). Bugs fixed on the way, each with a test: Force Bubble, Phytohydra and Lichenthrope let unpreventable damage through; entering-counter aggregates had no source; sacrificed tokens were offered to graveyard-exile costs; a reveal could hang on a token in a library; hasKeyword flashback matched jump-start; the card-type filter read printed types on the battlefield; SBAs ran before an as-attached choice; mills could take a put-back card twice; a declined commander went to the library bottom on a shuffle. Left: the majors and user calls from B334, and Drain Power (a forced mana-ability decision, major).",
